{"name":"Longlure Frogfish","hex":"#ebd84b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frogfish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any fish of the genus Lophius.","Any of several benthic anglerfish, of the family Antennariidae, having a frog-like mouth with a lure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frogfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Longlure frogfish","blocks":[{"text":"The longlure frogfish, also known as the flagpole frogfish, is a species of marine ray-finned fish belonging to the family Antennariidae, the frogfishes. This species is found in the western Atlantic. The longlure frogfish mimics its background habitat of sponges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Antennarius_multiocellatus_SI.jpg/330px-Antennarius_multiocellatus_SI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longlure_frogfish","wikidata":"Q141664"},{"title":"Frogfish","blocks":[{"text":"Frogfishes are any member of the anglerfish family Antennariidae, of the order Lophiiformes. Antennariids are known as anglerfish in Australia, where the term \"frogfish\" refers to members of the unrelated family Batrachoididae. Frogfishes are found in almost all tropical and subtropical oceans and seas around the world, the primary exception being the Mediterranean Sea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Antennarius_striatus_%288492976355%29.jpg/330px-Antennarius_striatus_%288492976355%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frogfish","wikidata":"Q540454"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longlure_frogfish_%28Antennarius_multiocellatus%29_twitching_lure.jpg/500px-Longlure_frogfish_%28Antennarius_multiocellatus%29_twitching_lure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed